Maintainer: Boswas OS Platform Team <os-platform@boswas.invalid>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), python3:any
Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: boswas-sysops
Architecture: all
Depends: apt,
         pkexec,
         polkitd,
         python3 (>= 3.11),
         ${misc:Depends}
Suggests: flatpak
Description: Boswas OS privileged helper for software, updates and runtimes
 The one privileged component behind Boswas Control Center's software,
 update, storage, hardware and Android pages. Started through pkexec as
 /usr/libexec/boswas/sysops <operation>, it performs a fixed set of
 operations, each with its own polkit action:
 .
  * APT: refresh, upgrade, install and remove packages from the configured,
    signature-verified repositories; install a local .deb (device policy)
  * cleanup: package cache, system journal
  * a read-only report of firmware the kernel could not find
  * approved Flatpak remotes
  * the Android runtime (Waydroid): install, initialise, update, repair,
    start and stop, from the Waydroid repository with its key pinned
 .
 It is never setuid, never a daemon, never runs a shell or an arbitrary
 command, refuses changes that would install software excluded by Boswas
 policy or remove protected packages, and reports progress and results as
 JSON Lines.
